\title{Tumor2Line: population-aware query-to-cell-line matching}
\description{
Tumor2Line provides a transcriptome-based workflow for matching tumor-derived
query populations to cancer cell lines using a scaled-PCA molecular
representation and population-aware unbalanced optimal transport.

Selecting cancer cell line models that faithfully represent patient tumors or other tumor-derived query samples is an important step toward improving the biological relevance and translational value of preclinical cancer studies. Tumor2Line provides a transcriptome-based framework for matching query populations, including tumors, patient-derived organoids, patient-derived xenografts, and related models, to candidate cancer cell lines. The workflow integrates expression preprocessing, a shared scaled principal component representation, and population-aware matching with unbalanced optimal transport. Known query-cell-line pairs are not required for matching and, when available, can be used to evaluate recovery with Top1 accuracy, Top3 accuracy, mean reciprocal rank, and true-pair rank. Visualization utilities support interpretation of candidate rankings and known-pair recovery.
}
